## 4.實例

• 君王為什麼需要講「君權神授」的故事？因為此時的神是天然的正當性源頭，將自己的權力包裝成「神的授權」，才能從神那裡借到正當性，成為「神選之人」，獲得最終的認同，也就是獲得了君王的權力進而才能成為君王。

• 君王為什麼會退出歷史的舞台？因為「君權神授」故事背景(生產力水平提升、對神的恐懼)發生了改變，這個故事已經變得牽強(講不好了，失去了正當性)，並且現實已經有更好的新故事，舊故事自然會被淘汰。

• 集權社會為什麼會高效？這不是因為「人多力量大」，而是因為集權實現了超大規模的信用共識場，所有人都被裹挾著講同一個故事，甚至變成萬眾一心的信仰。(當然了，高效僅僅是高效的意思，吃好穿好會高效，吃不好穿不上也會高效；生產創造會高效，破壞毀滅也會高效，歷史早就證明，追求極致高效最終會被高效毀滅。其本質原因是意識不受現實限制，載體的結算又總是延遲，在當今技術加速的推動下，自毀也已然被加速)。

• 現代國家的民主制度為什麼是授權體制？因為從神權到王權再到現代法制的歷史進程中，講故事的人在發生變化→從少數到大眾化；故事的正當性也在變化→從神權王權敘事失效到「人權」敘事興起；在這一過程中，新興敘事還編織不出一部去中心化的劇本，仍還需要一個中心化的權力載體來「代表」大家授權。所以民主看起來是人民當家，實際還是把話語權集中在少數人手上。

• 人為什麼會想要控制話語權？因為就如「會哭的孩子有奶吃」一樣，哭出正當性，哭到被認可接受，就會取得額外的利益；為什麼總有些人即使有能力也會被動，而另一些人動動嘴就可以掌握主動？僅動動嘴肯定不行，能行的是控制敘事框架的話語權者，其權力比能力暴力了無數倍。


一切社會現實，都可以在正當性敘事中解釋，更能在正當性敘事中解決，這就是社會結構作為虛擬敘事的必然邏輯。在這個意義上，語言的邊界，確實就是文明的邊界、世界的邊界。

## 4.Example

• Why did kings need to tell the story of “divine right of kings”? Because at that time, God was the natural source of legitimacy. By packaging their power as “authorized by God,” they could borrow legitimacy from God, become “God's chosen one,” gain ultimate recognition, and thereby obtain the Quanli of kingship and actually become king.
• Why did kings exit the stage of history? Because the background of the “divine right” story changed (productivity improved, fear of gods diminished), the story became strained (no longer well-told, lost legitimacy), and reality already had better new stories. Old stories are naturally eliminated.
• Why were centralized societies efficient? Not because “more people means more power,” but because centralization achieved an ultra-large-scale credit consensus field: everyone was swept up in telling the same story, even turning into unanimous faith. (Of course, efficiency is merely efficiency — eating well and dressing well is efficient; eating poorly and going naked is also efficient; production and creation are efficient; destruction and ruin are also efficient. History has long proven that the pursuit of ultimate efficiency ultimately gets destroyed by efficiency itself. The essential reason is that consciousness is unbound by reality, while carrier settlement is always deferred. Under today's technological acceleration, self-destruction has already been accelerated.)
• Why is the democratic system of modern states an authorization regime? Because in the historical progression from divine right to royal right to modern law, the people telling the story changed — from a minority to mass participation; the legitimacy of the story also changed — from divine/royal right narratives losing validity to “human rights” narratives rising. In this process, emerging narratives could not yet weave a fully decentralized script and still needed a centralized Quanli carrier to “represent” everyone in authorization. Thus, democracy appears to be rule by the people, but in reality, discursive power remains concentrated in the hands of a few.
• Why do people want to control discursive power? Because, just like “the squeaky wheel gets the grease,” crying out legitimacy — crying until it is recognized and accepted — brings extra benefits. Why are some people passive even when capable, while others can seize the initiative just by moving their lips? Merely moving lips is certainly not enough; what works is discursive power that controls the narrative framework — its Quanli is countless times more violent than capability.

All social realities can be explained within legitimacy narrative and even solved within legitimacy narrative — this is the inevitable logic of social structure as virtual narrative. In this sense, the boundaries of language are indeed the boundaries of civilization and the boundaries of the world.

