## 5.權力消除的假象
​
在物理世界中，種子總有發芽的權力，重力總有發生的權力，生命總有代謝的權力。除非其結構毀滅，否則這些權力確定存在，其權力關係純粹而直接，無需承認、無需維持、無需二次審核。
在人類社會中，意識的主觀意志對現實的模仿虛構、對現實的承認或否認、甚至完全不在乎真實的虛構，在「意識與載體的非對稱關係——這一無法逾越的天壑」面前，只能將原本一體的世界割裂為思想與物質的二元態。這既是常常互相製造困擾的對立態，也是你中有我、我中有你的融合態，從而使得社會權力關係呈現出複雜而混亂的特徵。

在這複雜而混亂的社會權力現實中，權利長期不被行使、職務變遷中的權力獲取與失效、財物所有權的轉移等現象普遍存在，但這些並非權力被消除的證據。

首先，權利不等同於權力，失去利益並非失去權力；財物所有權的改變僅為權力載體的更替，權力本身並未消失。職務變遷中，權力附屬於職務符號而非個人，例如總統的權力屬於「總統」這一符號，而非承載該符號的個體。其次，社會中常見不承認天然權力的現象，例如無視環境極限或種子發芽的權力。此時，這些天然權力在人為「帳本」上被視為已消除，但這僅是債務掛帳：環境極限終將發生，種子發芽的權力直至死亡為止；正如被阻斷的水流，雖然其當下流動能力受限，但仍然具有流動的權力。即便宣稱剝奪了政治或人身權力，事實是被剝奪者的能力被剝奪，就是說他失去了主張其政治或人身權力的能力，而權力從未消失；換一個角度來看，如果说權力剝奪真實發生了，那麼對該個體而言，原有社會結構已毀壞。再如神權，它並未消失，而是在神權為組成部分的社會結構中存續；在不承認神的社會中，神權結正當性已不在，神權社會結構已被破壞。若現有的社會中仍有神存在（無論真實存在還是被承認存在），那麼神權仍然存在，例如現實宗教中的神。

良俗或陋習都是社會性權力的顯化，社會文化是其最重要的遺傳工具，只要文化不變，習俗就不會滅。無論對受侵害者還是受益者，習俗均在其文化中獲取了現實正當性，即社會權力。習俗退出歷史舞台，並非因為正義、文明，而是權力的消失：以舊有習俗為正當的載體消失了，即承載文化遺傳的載體不在了，使得舊有習俗的社會結構崩潰了。

社會權力，是社會結構的組成部分，除非毀滅它不會消失，它的反饋也不會消失，它會被整個社會在某一觸點承擔。而權力一旦消失，即代表了社會結構的崩裂，也就會成為載體毀滅性的災難。因此，每一次社會結構的變遷，本質上都是權力的更迭，文明進化史就是一部毀滅與重構的變更史。每一次毀滅與重構都在血腥掠奪中開始，又在奴役鬥爭中結束，並且，所有掠奪與奴役都會用敘事披上「正義」這一正當性外衣，以文明進步的權力實施。

意識作為外來介入者，其對現實有著本能的不真實感（意識不直接參與物理真實結算），常會主觀無視天然權力，或陷入到「意識決定物質」的自大中。它以為修改法律、改變說法，即可改變現實。然而載體本體唯有誠實：敘事過度透支，載體會生病、不育、抑鬱、死亡，這是意識在現實中最真實的無奈。
載體與物理現實的反饋，終究需由整個社會結構承擔，此時，能與物理規律對齊的科學敘事，就會成為透支消費的「超級槓桿」，槓桿越大，掛帳規模越大。伴隨科技及其加速的到來，反饋將愈發強烈與快速，呈幾何倍數增長的結算力量，終將會超物理極限爆發。

意識無視天然權力的行為，對載體而言或許是現實痛苦的根源，而對意識本體而言，卻會成為逃避結算的生存策略。

## 5.The Illusion of Quanli Elimination

In the physical world, a seed always has the Quanli to sprout, gravity always has the Quanli to act, life always has the Quanli to metabolize. Unless its structure is destroyed, these Quanli exist definitively, their Quanli relationships pure and direct, requiring no recognition, no maintenance, no secondary verification.
In human society, consciousness's subjective will — through imitation and fabrication of reality, recognition or denial of reality, or even complete disregard for truth — can only split the originally unified world into a binary of thought and matter in the face of the “asymmetrical relationship between consciousness and carriers — this unbridgeable chasm.” This is both an oppositional state that often creates mutual trouble and a fused state of mutual containment, resulting in the complex and chaotic characteristics of social Quanli relationships.

In this complex and chaotic reality of social Quanli, phenomena such as rights long unexercised, power gained and lost during job transitions, and transfer of property ownership are widespread, but these are not evidence of Quanli being eliminated.

First, rights are not equivalent to Quanli; loss of benefit is not loss of Quanli. Change in property ownership is merely a change in Quanli carrier; Quanli itself does not disappear. In job transitions, Quanli attaches to the position symbol rather than the individual — for example, the power of the president belongs to the symbol “president,” not to the person carrying that symbol. Second, society commonly features non-recognition of Tianran Quanli, such as disregarding environmental limits or the Quanli of seed germination. At such times, these Tianran Quanli are treated as eliminated on the artificial “ledger,” but this is only debt on account: environmental limits will eventually manifest, the Quanli of seed germination persists until death; just like blocked water flow — though its current flow capacity is restricted, it still possesses the Quanli to flow. Even when political or personal Quanli is declared deprived, in fact it is the deprived person's capacity that is deprived — meaning they have lost the capacity to assert their political or personal Quanli, while Quanli itself never disappears. From another perspective, if Quanli deprivation truly occurred, then for that individual the original social structure has already been destroyed. Likewise, divine Quanli has not disappeared; it persists in social structures where divine Quanli is a component. In societies that do not recognize God, divine Quanli legitimacy no longer exists, and divine-right social structures have been destroyed. If God still exists in the current society (whether truly existing or recognized as existing), then divine Quanli still exists — for example, in real-world religions.

Good customs or bad habits are both manifestations of social Quanli; social culture is their most important hereditary tool. As long as the culture remains unchanged, customs will not die out. Whether for the harmed or the beneficiaries, customs acquire real legitimacy within their culture — that is, social Quanli. Customs exit the historical stage not because of justice or civilization, but because Quanli disappears: the carriers who regarded the old customs as legitimate have vanished — that is, the carriers carrying cultural inheritance are gone, causing the social structure of the old customs to collapse.

Social Quanli is a component of social structure; unless destroyed, it does not disappear, nor does its feedback disappear. It will be borne by the entire society at certain touchpoints. When Quanli disappears, it signifies the rupture of social structure, which becomes a catastrophic disaster for carriers. Therefore, every transformation of social structure is essentially a change of Quanli; the history of civilizational evolution is a history of destruction and reconstruction. Every destruction and reconstruction begins in bloody plunder and ends in enslavement struggle, and all plunder and enslavement are cloaked in the legitimacy garment of “justice” through narrative, implemented with the Quanli of civilizational progress.

As an external intervener, consciousness has an instinctive sense of unreality toward reality (consciousness does not directly participate in physical real settlement), often subjectively ignoring Tianran Quanli or falling into the arrogance of “consciousness determines matter.” It believes that changing laws or changing words can change reality. However, the carrier ontology is only honest: when narrative is over-leveraged, carriers become ill, infertile, depressed, and die — this is consciousness's most real helplessness in reality.
The feedback from carriers and physical reality must ultimately be borne by the entire social structure. At this point, scientific narrative — the only one that aligns with physical laws — becomes the “super leverage” for overdraft consumption. The greater the leverage, the larger the account on hold. With the arrival of technology and its acceleration, feedback will become increasingly intense and rapid; settlement force growing geometrically will ultimately explode beyond physical limits.

Consciousness's behavior of disregarding Tianran Quanli may be the root of real suffering for carriers, but for consciousness itself, it becomes a survival strategy to evade settlement.

